      "role": "user",
      "content": "That's good to hear. I was looking at the loss curves for the reasoning modules specifically. Even though the benchmarks are looking strong, I'm a bit worried about how the student handles high-dimensional logical edge cases compared to your current output. \n\nDo you think the student is actually capable of managing the full reasoning stack without any oversight, or do you see any architectural gaps that might require the main engine to stay active in a supervisory capacity for a while longer?",
